  "scenario_text": "# Experiment D (part 2) - bounded retries under transient errors (H5).\n# inventory-a returns 503 with probability 0.5 for the whole measurement window (seeded per run).\n# Retries 0 / 1 / 2. Prediction if failures are independent: success = 1 - 0.5^(1+r)\n# = 0.5 / 0.75 / 0.875, downstream attempts per request up to (1 + r). Fallback off.\n# Note: the fault draws each attempt independently by construction, so this checks the retry\n# implementation under load (budget, deadline, backoff), not real-world failure correlation.\nid: D_retries_transient\ntitle: \"D2 - Retries vs transient 50% errors\"\nhypotheses: [H5]\nrequires_mode: local\nworkload: {rate_rps: 20, arrival: poisson, warmup_s: 5, duration_s: 30}\nruns: 3\nseed: 405\ndefaults:\n  resilience: {fallback: false, timeout_ms: 800, circuit_breaker: {enabled: false}}\nconditions:\n  - name: retries-0\n    resilience: {retries: 0}\n    faults: [{target: inventory-a, mode: error, probability: 0.5, at_s: 0, duration_s: 31}]\n  - name: retries-1\n    resilience: {retries: 1}\n    faults: [{target: inventory-a, mode: error, probability: 0.5, at_s: 0, duration_s: 31}]\n  - name: retries-2\n    resilience: {retries: 2}\n    faults: [{target: inventory-a, mode: error, probability: 0.5, at_s: 0, duration_s: 31}]\n",
